.TH env_make 3
.SH NAME
env_make \- populate an environment pointer array
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B int env_make(const char** \fIv\fP, size_t \fIargc\fP, const char* \fIs\fP, size_t \fIlen\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_make
populates the array \fIv\fP with pointers to strings located within the buffer \fIs\fP. 
It expects a series of null-terminated strings packed sequentially in \fIs\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if \fIargc\fP exceeds the bounds of \fIlen\fP (sets \fIerrno\fP to EINVAL).